1
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:06,700
Huh?

2
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:13,659
The bread I bought has been mysteriously
replaced by three 100-yen coins.

3
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,040
Do I take that as
a sign of sincerity?

4
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:19,500
Tohsaka.

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,510
Tohsaka!

6
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,180
You in here?

7
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:30,680
I wonder what this is.

8
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,940
Sorry.

9
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:41,940
I'll be... just a
little longer...

10
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,615
Soy

11
00:00:48,616 --> 00:00:50,280
Oyster

12
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:50,280
Shirou, how are you feeling?

13
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:53,539
The numbness on
my left side is gone.

14
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:56,249
It still feels a little
heavy, though.

15
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:57,790
That is good news.

16
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:01,800
Good morning, Rin.

17
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:03,419
Morning.

18
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:06,589
You seem to have slept
quite soundly last night.

19
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:13,060
Not really. Somebody kept
making noise well past midnight.

20
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:16,139
Oh, and we're going out today.

21
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:17,480
Hurry up and get ready.

22
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:20,649
Going out? Where?

23
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:22,320
The next town over.

24
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:23,899
To do what?

25
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,820
What else? To go
have fun, of course.

26
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,160
It's a date, dummy.

27
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:31,699
A date?

28
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,659
Between who and who?

29
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,660
Me and you.

30
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,409
Oh, okay.

31
00:01:37,410 --> 00:01:38,999
You and me, huh...

32
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:39,500
Wh...

33
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,000
Whaaat?

34
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:59,230
In the face of absolute despair

35
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:03,230
That nearly burned
our hearts away

36
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:09,780
You still found the
courage to smile

37
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:14,580
Like you accepted it all

38
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:17,840
I lost my voice

39
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:20,460
And the things I wanted to say

40
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:25,710
But every time I
fell to my knees

41
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:30,010
I stood up and kept walking

42
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:35,680
We were looking for
the ideal white future

43
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:40,910
Our one and only hope

44
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:43,400
Now I may be left with nothing

45
00:02:43,570 --> 00:02:48,820
But these raging
emotions that have

46
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,920
Nowhere to go

47
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:57,170
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

48
00:02:57,550 --> 00:03:00,580
With more than one right answer

49
00:03:00,820 --> 00:03:04,410
I won't stop

50
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:06,440
Until I find it

51
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:15,850
Shirou?

52
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:19,640
What's this about you going
on a date with Tohsaka-san?

53
00:03:19,641 --> 00:03:20,980
The Final Decision

54
00:03:20,981 --> 00:03:22,190
This is your big chance!

55
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:24,559
Stop messing around.

56
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,689
I don't know what's
going on here, either.

57
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:30,069
Look at you, getting
all embarrassed!

58
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:33,200
I'm so jealous! Oh,
to be young again!

59
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:37,280
You have a date today too,
don't you, Fujimura-sensei?

60
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:38,869
You do?

61
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:40,870
Yep, sure do.

62
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:44,829
But that doesn't mean you two
can get carried away, all right?

63
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:46,590
See you later!

64
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:50,339
We should go too.

65
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,340
Indeed.

66
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:06,519
So, where should we go?

67
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,400
Do you two have any requests?

68
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:11,529
Don't ask me.

69
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:14,069
Should've known. And you, Saber?

70
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:17,489
No. I am merely here
as Shirou's guard.

71
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:20,159
Please act as though
I am not present.

72
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:25,420
Really? Then you two are okay with
completely submitting to my every whim?

73
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:27,959
Don't be so sinister!

74
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:33,379
Anyway, I said I'd tag along with
you, not go out on a date with you.

75
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:36,339
I thought it might be nice
for us to take a breather.

76
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:38,180
Let me stop you there.

77
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:37,550
All three of us.

78
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:41,389
That happens to be
what people call a "date."

79
00:04:41,390 --> 00:04:44,429
You won't be very popular if
you don't know when to give in.

80
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,939
With who?

81
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:49,730
Who, indeed?

82
00:04:50,730 --> 00:04:51,730
Shirou.

83
00:04:53,780 --> 00:04:55,569
Fine, whatever!

84
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:58,300
I'll tag along with you
wherever you want, then!

85
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:06,960
Well? Is it good?

86
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:10,879
Uh... I can't really tell.

87
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:14,380
What? I'm sure you can
tell it's sweet, at least!

88
00:05:15,050 --> 00:05:19,220
Well, I guess it is way
sweeter than it looks.

89
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,080
Well?

90
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,669
Well what?

91
00:05:50,670 --> 00:05:52,789
They're not bad, I guess.

92
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:56,129
Yes. They make you
look intellectual, Rin.

93
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:57,509
Thanks!

94
00:05:57,510 --> 00:05:58,970
Now, which next...

95
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:02,430
I think these would
look good on you, Saber.

96
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:08,940
Looking good! And you
try these on, Emiya-kun!

97
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,360
That's hilarious!

98
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:24,119
I will never, ever
wear glasses, got it?

99
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,330
I look young enough already!

100
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:29,459
Oh, right.

101
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,120
You're self-conscious
about that.

102
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:35,459
I don't think you have anything
to worry about, Emiya-kun.

103
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:37,460
You're perfectly
fine as you are.

104
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:40,179
No, I'm not!

105
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:43,889
I have to grow a little taller.

106
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:45,560
You're pretty average, I'd say.

107
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:47,889
I'm nowhere near average!

108
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:51,269
I have to grow at
least as tall as Issei!

109
00:06:51,270 --> 00:06:55,820
Don't worry about it. You'll
grow plenty taller, I'm sure.

110
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,030
Based on what?

111
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:05,030
Um, you've got a solid build, so
I bet you'll fill out if you eat right.

112
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:09,329
With plenty of photosynthesis,
you'll grow nice and tall!

113
00:07:09,330 --> 00:07:10,330
I think.

114
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:14,289
Do I look like I have leaves?

115
00:07:14,290 --> 00:07:16,800
Wait, are you angry?

116
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:20,880
Not really. I'll take your
advice with a grain of salt.

117
00:07:21,130 --> 00:07:23,839
I can't make you any
promises about your height,

118
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,550
but I'm sure you'll become
a great-looking guy.

119
00:07:26,850 --> 00:07:29,980
You have my guarantee
on that part, Shirou.

120
00:07:31,850 --> 00:07:33,729
Ooh, you're blushing!

121
00:07:33,730 --> 00:07:36,360
I love how everything is
written on your face, Emiya-kun.

122
00:07:37,150 --> 00:07:38,649
Geez, you're evil!

123
00:07:38,650 --> 00:07:42,609
Do you get your kicks from teasing
guys in the same year as you?

124
00:07:42,610 --> 00:07:43,909
Of course!

125
00:07:43,910 --> 00:07:46,410
You have the best reactions!

126
00:07:47,030 --> 00:07:51,449
Let's stop playing with Shirou
and start on the main event!

127
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:54,460
Before lunch, let's knock
a few out of the park!

128
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,550
Take that!

129
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,050
One more time!

130
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:02,590
That machine's set to 120 kph...

131
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:07,179
Shirou, what are you
standing around for?

132
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:09,890
Yeah, I can't let Tohsaka
steal the spotlight!

133
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,400
Saber?

134
00:08:28,830 --> 00:08:31,539
Wh-What is it, Shirou?

135
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:34,410
I find it uncomfortable to be
stared at in such a manner.

136
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:37,420
Talk about hating to lose.

137
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:39,879
I miscalculated.

138
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:43,760
I had no idea Saber
would be so competitive.

139
00:08:44,130 --> 00:08:49,010
Yeah, she gets angry if you go easy on her,
and she sulks if you get too far ahead...

140
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:54,429
Y-You were just as eager to
compete against Rin, Shirou!

141
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:59,229
When the person in the next cage
is going nuts, you get worked up too.

142
00:08:59,230 --> 00:09:02,530
And seriously, you're way
too good at batting, Tohsaka.

143
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:06,780
Do you do pushups before
going to bed or something?

144
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:12,039
Y-Yes, I do.

145
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,200
What's wrong with that?

146
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,169
Uh, nothing.

147
00:09:17,170 --> 00:09:18,210
Good game.

148
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:30,219
Wow. You put way more
effort into this than I expected.

149
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:32,059
Of course.

150
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:35,730
When I ask someone
out, I don't kid around.

151
00:09:36,230 --> 00:09:38,979
Oh, that explains one mystery.

152
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:41,939
This is what you
used the bread for.

153
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:48,029
I figured you'd just scarfed the
whole loaf as a midnight snack.

154
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:49,530
Emiya-kun?

155
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:54,619
Shut your mouth, and let's eat.

156
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:56,249
Oh. Right.

157
00:09:56,250 --> 00:09:57,460
Let's eat.

158
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,000
Thank you for the meal, Rin.

159
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:08,879
Huh? Do you not like
spicy food, Shirou?

160
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:11,389
No, I'm okay.

161
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:14,600
The seasoning is intense,
but this is really good!

162
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,600
Oh? I'm glad.

163
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:20,520
You've got some
ketchup on your face.

164
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,060
Shall I get that for you?

165
00:10:23,770 --> 00:10:26,820
Wh-Why would you say that?

166
00:10:28,530 --> 00:10:31,820
Oops. Maybe I
took the joke too far.

167
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:37,500
Sorry! I knew exactly the reaction
I'd get, so I couldn't help myself.

168
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:41,579
Whatever. But just you wait.

169
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:44,670
I'll be cool as a cucumber
from tomorrow on.

170
00:10:45,130 --> 00:10:50,009
Oh? Does that mean I can start
going after you with everything I have?

171
00:10:50,010 --> 00:10:54,600
What a relief! I was so
sick of taking it easy on you.

172
00:10:54,930 --> 00:10:56,929
Uh, I take that back.

173
00:10:56,930 --> 00:10:59,395
I'll need a little more
time, so if you could

174
00:10:59,407 --> 00:11:01,939
keep it at our current
level, that'd be great.

175
00:11:01,940 --> 00:11:05,019
Really? If you say so.

176
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:07,439
But when you're ready to
step up your game, let me know.

177
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:10,029
I'll stop pulling my punches
and knock you on your butt.

178
00:11:10,030 --> 00:11:12,029
You're that sure
you'll win, huh?

179
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:14,989
Are you sure you're
not the Devil herself?

180
00:11:14,990 --> 00:11:16,660
I mean, you're
always wearing red.

181
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:22,539
You look like
you're feeling better.

182
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:24,080
Guess you're back to normal.

183
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,960
I'm glad.

184
00:11:31,550 --> 00:11:32,799
Tohsaka.

185
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,969
What?

186
00:11:33,970 --> 00:11:37,059
Why did you come over yesterday?

187
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:39,269
Let alone sleep over.

188
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:41,479
Why?

189
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,229
I felt like it, that's all.

190
00:11:43,230 --> 00:11:45,650
I thought it might be
a nice change of pace.

191
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:50,029
Well, it was fun to
have lots of people over.

192
00:11:50,030 --> 00:11:51,030
Right?

193
00:11:51,280 --> 00:11:55,620
Yeah. It ended up being nothing
special, but thanks anyway.

194
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:59,909
D-Don't get the wrong idea!

195
00:11:59,910 --> 00:12:03,999
I-I wasn't concerned about you!

196
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,919
Yeah, you'd be at a disadvantage
if you lost your partner.

197
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:08,749
So you came to see
how I was doing, right?

198
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:11,459
Th-That's right! I'm
glad you understand.

199
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:14,129
Yeah. I appreciate it.

200
00:12:14,130 --> 00:12:19,720
I don't know what you were after, but
you really were concerned, weren't you?

201
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:38,280
That boy Shirou is going
on dates now, bold as can be.

202
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:42,949
Oh, and get this, Kiritsugu-san. Do
you remember a girl named Saber-chan?

203
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:45,540
She says she's the daughter
of someone you knew abroad.

204
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:49,380
Came all this way to visit you.

205
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:54,340
Abroad, huh?

206
00:12:55,800 --> 00:13:00,810
We never got the chance
to go on a trip, huh?

207
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:24,040
We made it.

208
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,580
Did you have fun today?

209
00:13:28,330 --> 00:13:30,999
We only got through
half of what I had planned,

210
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,050
but how did you like it?

211
00:13:32,590 --> 00:13:37,380
Well, I haven't goofed
around like that for a long time.

212
00:13:38,470 --> 00:13:42,509
Look, if you had fun,
just come out and say so.

213
00:13:42,510 --> 00:13:45,230
The least you can do is tell me
straight after I played host all day.

214
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:48,269
Sorry. I didn't mean to be rude.

215
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:49,399
Yes, you did.

216
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:52,360
You're subconsciously
slamming on the brakes.

217
00:13:53,730 --> 00:13:55,859
I don't know what
happened to you,

218
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:59,530
but if it was that bad, wouldn't your
life be a lot happier if you let it go?

219
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:11,000
Shirou, look outside.

220
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,169
Is something wrong?

221
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:17,010
I don't know. It's weird.

222
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,180
What?

223
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:54,420
What is this place?

224
00:14:55,170 --> 00:14:58,630
I can't get through to Archer.
We're completely sealed in.

225
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:15,860
These are...

226
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:37,549
This is only serving to
increase their number.

227
00:15:37,550 --> 00:15:39,340
Precisely.

228
00:15:40,010 --> 00:15:45,050
Fighting within my magic field will
only expend your mana to no avail.

229
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:50,429
You're pulling out all
the stops for us, I see.

230
00:15:50,430 --> 00:15:53,899
As long as there's water, you have
an endless supply of troops, huh?

231
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:56,360
We cut them off
at the source, then.

232
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:59,069
How valiant.

233
00:15:59,070 --> 00:16:04,700
But perhaps you ought to look at this
before you raise your sword at me, Saber.

234
00:16:12,370 --> 00:16:13,370
Fuji-nee!

235
00:16:19,170 --> 00:16:22,300
What do you hope to
accomplish by taking a hostage?

236
00:16:22,590 --> 00:16:25,009
I have no business with you.

237
00:16:25,010 --> 00:16:27,890
My interest lies
with that boy there.

238
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:31,219
Your magic circuits
are fascinating.

239
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,479
I'd like to take them without
killing you, if possible.

240
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,979
Do you understand?

241
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:38,004
I'm resorting to these
crude tactics because

242
00:16:38,016 --> 00:16:40,569
I wish to win you
over, not kill you.

243
00:16:40,570 --> 00:16:43,319
If you become my puppet,

244
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:45,909
I shall refrain from
any further violence.

245
00:16:45,910 --> 00:16:50,410
Listen to you! You're doing all
this behind your Master's back!

246
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:52,659
Is that jealousy I hear?

247
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:57,169
I hate to disappoint you, but it is
not perfect omnipotence that I desire,

248
00:16:57,170 --> 00:17:00,709
but rather imperfect,
unique abilities.

249
00:17:00,710 --> 00:17:03,670
So, boy, what is your answer?

250
00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:11,969
Such a difficult child. This
should be an easy decision.

251
00:17:11,970 --> 00:17:14,849
No matter how
skilled your Saber is,

252
00:17:14,850 --> 00:17:18,560
she cannot defeat me with
my limitless reserves of mana.

253
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:23,609
My power is being fed to
me by all who live in this city.

254
00:17:23,610 --> 00:17:26,819
It is as though I have
thousands of Masters.

255
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:29,239
Do you understand
what I am saying?

256
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:31,159
You wouldn't dare!

257
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:37,419
So you do. Even humans who are
devoid of mana still have souls, yes?

258
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:40,629
And we are soul eaters
by nature, are we not?

259
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:43,549
By stealing mana in the
form of life from these Masters,

260
00:17:43,550 --> 00:17:46,170
I can extract as much as I like.

261
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:52,009
Listen, boy, you have
no chance of winning.

262
00:17:52,010 --> 00:17:54,720
Serve me alongside Saber.

263
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,730
Let Fuji-nee go!

264
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:04,109
Weren't you listening?

265
00:18:04,110 --> 00:18:06,650
I said to surrender to me.

266
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:09,570
Like hell I will!
Let Fuji-nee go!

267
00:18:12,070 --> 00:18:15,909
So you have no interest in
working with another Master?

268
00:18:15,910 --> 00:18:18,749
No, just not with you.

269
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:22,129
I seem to be on your bad side.

270
00:18:22,130 --> 00:18:24,249
That really is a shame.

271
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:27,169
Had you worked with me,

272
00:18:27,170 --> 00:18:30,049
I would have been willing
to share the Grail with you.

273
00:18:30,050 --> 00:18:32,679
I don't care about that.

274
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:35,970
I promised myself that I'd
fight to stop people like you.

275
00:18:36,430 --> 00:18:38,520
The Grail is irrelevant!

276
00:18:44,270 --> 00:18:45,730
What's so funny?

277
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:48,489
Oh, did I strike a nerve?

278
00:18:48,490 --> 00:18:53,070
But you have only yourself to blame,
saying things that you don't mean.

279
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,949
After all, you yourself
are a victim of the Grail.

280
00:18:56,950 --> 00:18:59,159
"The Grail is irrelevant"...

281
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:04,170
The reason you reject it so
strongly is out of hatred, is it not?

282
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,500
Shirou?

283
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:09,969
I know all about
you, Emiya Shirou.

284
00:19:09,970 --> 00:19:14,010
You lost everything
in the last war.

285
00:19:14,850 --> 00:19:21,270
You were found by Emiya Kiritsugu as you
lay alone in the flames, waiting to die.

286
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:25,346
And you were made his
son, magic forced upon you,

287
00:19:25,358 --> 00:19:28,900
solely for the next war.
How you must have suffered.

288
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:31,279
No way...

289
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:33,909
Emiya-kun? Is that true?

290
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:39,499
Yes, the Grail has always
been a hated enemy to you.

291
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:42,729
It is for that very reason
that you have every right

292
00:19:42,741 --> 00:19:45,919
to claim the Grail as
recompense for ten years ago.

293
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:49,259
And the Grail is
as good as mine.

294
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:52,760
It would be child's play
to grant you your wish.

295
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:54,969
You speak nonsense, Caster!

296
00:19:54,970 --> 00:19:59,100
The Grail will not appear
until but one Servant remains!

297
00:19:59,470 --> 00:20:04,939
No, there is a way to
claim it without fighting.

298
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:08,940
As a Caster, I can sense
the inner workings of the Grail.

299
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:14,950
Yes, if you, with your massive
mana output, were to assist me,

300
00:20:16,030 --> 00:20:19,700
I could summon the
Grail here and now.

301
00:20:22,410 --> 00:20:25,539
This is your last chance, boy.

302
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:28,249
You wish to avoid senseless
fighting, do you not?

303
00:20:28,250 --> 00:20:30,340
Then serve me,

304
00:20:30,710 --> 00:20:32,630
Saber's Master!

305
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,389
Never.

306
00:20:40,390 --> 00:20:42,430
I reject your offer.

307
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:45,559
Are you mad?

308
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:48,479
Do you understand
the position you are in?

309
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,900
I won't help a witch who
treats people as food.

310
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,649
Your methods are wrong.

311
00:20:54,650 --> 00:20:56,160
And one more thing...

312
00:20:56,410 --> 00:20:59,659
I wasn't forced to
become a mage.

313
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:02,950
I chose on my own to follow
in my old man's footsteps.

314
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:08,420
Witch... You called me a witch?

315
00:21:08,830 --> 00:21:12,089
I see. I have no
use for you, then.

316
00:21:12,090 --> 00:21:14,169
You can die here!

317
00:21:14,170 --> 00:21:15,090
Why, you...

318
00:21:15,091 --> 00:21:16,590
Don't do it, Saber!

319
00:21:18,090 --> 00:21:19,090
I'm begging you.

320
00:21:19,930 --> 00:21:21,180
Stay where you are.

321
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,810
Shirou, but she...

322
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:36,110
Oh, my. I had thought that
you were utterly irrational,

323
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:39,780
but you do understand
your situation, don't you?

324
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:42,199
Coward!

325
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,290
You're going to kill
Shirou in cold blood?

326
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:49,120
Of course not. I'm merely going to
strip him of his status as a Master.

327
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:53,709
You will not join me, but
you wish to save this girl.

328
00:21:53,710 --> 00:21:58,130
That tells me that you are prepared
to hand over your Command Spells.

329
00:22:00,890 --> 00:22:04,389
All right. How do I do that?

330
00:22:04,390 --> 00:22:07,230
Shirou, no! She won't stop...

331
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:11,230
I will take them, of
course. Arm and all.

332
00:22:12,230 --> 00:22:14,649
That is enough, Shirou.

333
00:22:14,650 --> 00:22:17,819
I cannot allow you to continue
to play into Caster's hands.

334
00:22:17,820 --> 00:22:19,529
Same here!

335
00:22:19,530 --> 00:22:23,330
I mean, do you honestly think she's
the sort who'd release a hostage?

336
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:29,579
Take it. That's all
you want, right?

337
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:30,500
Shirou!

338
00:22:30,501 --> 00:22:33,919
You don't have to go to
such extremes to help others!

339
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:34,920
I do!

340
00:22:35,750 --> 00:22:38,062
If giving up my arm
will save Fuji-nee's

341
00:22:38,074 --> 00:22:40,630
life, I'll do it without
a second's thought.

342
00:22:49,270 --> 00:22:51,520
You truly are a foolish child!

343
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:55,070
You are a nuisance, so die!

344
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:03,239
No! Stop!

345
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,490
Saber!

346
00:23:19,210 --> 00:23:20,470
Saber!

347
00:23:36,860 --> 00:23:38,529
Are you surprised?

348
00:23:38,530 --> 00:23:42,449
This is my Noble
Phantasm, Rule Breaker!

349
00:23:42,450 --> 00:23:46,579
It nullifies any and all
magic cast in this world.

350
00:23:46,580 --> 00:23:48,870
The dagger of
betrayal and denial.

351
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:51,579
The pact has been forged.

352
00:23:51,580 --> 00:23:53,620
I am now your Master.

353
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:56,289
You are now as I am.

354
00:23:56,290 --> 00:23:59,880
Betray your Master, and
pledge your blade to me!

355
00:24:02,340 --> 00:24:05,889
You... You took a Servant,
despite being one yourself?

356
00:24:05,890 --> 00:24:08,849
Yes, I have made
her my familiar.

357
00:24:08,850 --> 00:24:11,430
Saber now belongs to me.

358
00:24:12,430 --> 00:24:16,109
And now I shall return
your friend, little fool.

359
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:17,110
Fuji-nee!

360
00:24:18,980 --> 00:24:21,860
Fuji-nee! Are you
okay? Fuji-nee!

361
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:24,700
Fuji-nee...

362
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:29,489
You know, I think
I shall let you go.

363
00:24:29,490 --> 00:24:34,579
That show you put on was so
wonderful it almost began to irritate me.

364
00:24:34,580 --> 00:24:35,580
However...

365
00:24:36,460 --> 00:24:41,089
Oh. I guess I should've
seen this coming.

366
00:24:41,090 --> 00:24:45,719
Yes. Playtime is
over, young lady.

367
00:24:45,720 --> 00:24:47,179
Now, Saber.

368
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:49,510
Strike down Archer's Master.

369
00:24:50,430 --> 00:24:53,350
Never! Who would
obey the likes of you?

370
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:58,149
No, you will obey, Saber.

371
00:24:58,150 --> 00:24:59,979
As long as I have
these Command Spells,

372
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:02,780
you cannot defy me
in either body or soul.

373
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,670
You idiot! Why did you do that?

374
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:21,419
What a pity.

375
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:25,550
Such a waste. That
boy was so fascinating.

376
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:29,050
Obey my Command Spell, Saber.

377
00:25:33,890 --> 00:25:35,560
Run...

378
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:40,690
Run, Shirou!

379
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:44,489
We have to get Fuji-nee...

380
00:25:44,490 --> 00:25:46,069
Just come on!

381
00:25:46,070 --> 00:25:47,399
Impossible!

382
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:51,700
Saber's magic resistance is even effective
against the binding of a Command Spell?

383
00:25:52,030 --> 00:25:54,500
But be that as it may,
I won't let you escape!

384
00:26:18,140 --> 00:26:19,389
It's about time!

385
00:26:19,390 --> 00:26:20,899
My apologies.

386
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:23,399
It took quite some time
to breach that magic field.

387
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,860
From the inside, however...

388
00:26:28,950 --> 00:26:30,740
Archer, take Fujimura-sensei!

389
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:33,990
Now, while we still can!

390
00:26:39,710 --> 00:26:40,790
Saber...

391
00:27:06,480 --> 00:27:08,570
Place Fujimura-sensei
in that room.

392
00:27:08,870 --> 00:27:11,090
Shirou, are you with me?

393
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:19,080
We're going to walk, okay?

394
00:27:26,090 --> 00:27:27,750
This was for the best.

395
00:27:28,340 --> 00:27:29,880
At least you're alive.

396
00:27:32,430 --> 00:27:35,890
For now, get some
rest, Emiya-kun.

397
00:27:43,190 --> 00:27:47,190
I see. Saber was taken while
I was busy breaching the field.

398
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:48,520
That's all you have to say?

399
00:27:49,150 --> 00:27:51,984
Yes. But we should
count our blessings that

400
00:27:51,996 --> 00:27:54,909
we now know what
Caster's Noble Phantasm is.

401
00:27:54,910 --> 00:27:58,950
That Caster... Always
sloppy on the follow-through.

402
00:27:59,370 --> 00:28:02,500
Deep down, she might
actually be a decent woman.

403
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:05,919
You don't seem very
concerned, Archer.

404
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:08,960
Weren't you rooting for Saber?

405
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:12,879
I don't recall ever
giving that impression.

406
00:28:12,880 --> 00:28:15,429
What makes you think that, Rin?

407
00:28:15,430 --> 00:28:19,769
Well... Would you believe me if
I said it was women's intuition?

408
00:28:19,770 --> 00:28:21,060
No.

409
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:23,890
For one, are you even old
enough to qualify as a woman?

410
00:28:24,810 --> 00:28:27,559
You are lacking in feminine
charms, to begin with,

411
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:30,940
not to mention
refinement. Furthermore...

412
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:36,950
and this is the most
damning—your appeal is hard to see.

413
00:28:39,740 --> 00:28:42,960
Well, well. You've finally
found your groove again,

414
00:28:46,330 --> 00:28:47,330
haven't you?

415
00:28:50,420 --> 00:28:53,299
Getting back to
the topic at hand,

416
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:57,889
here's my first piece of evidence
that you were rooting for Saber:

417
00:28:57,890 --> 00:29:01,220
the first time you met her,
you went easy, didn't you?

418
00:29:02,140 --> 00:29:04,599
No matter how powerful Saber is,

419
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:08,020
I doubt she could have gotten the
better of you. Not with your defenses.

420
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:11,569
She caught me unawares.

421
00:29:11,570 --> 00:29:15,489
Like you, I'm vulnerable to
unexpected developments.

422
00:29:15,490 --> 00:29:17,699
Oh, get off my case.

423
00:29:17,700 --> 00:29:20,489
The second piece of evidence:

424
00:29:20,490 --> 00:29:24,579
after the incident with Rider, you
tried to provoke Saber, remember?

425
00:29:24,580 --> 00:29:28,170
That was out of character
for you, no two ways about it.

426
00:29:28,790 --> 00:29:32,000
But when I looked at it from
another angle, it made perfect sense.

427
00:29:32,380 --> 00:29:35,630
You were actually
scolding Saber, weren't you?

428
00:29:37,050 --> 00:29:40,469
I'm right? I knew it!

429
00:29:40,470 --> 00:29:43,150
I don't know if you two knew
each other in a previous life or what,

430
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:47,519
but it's unusual for you
to be so cold to someone.

431
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:53,110
Is it? As far as I'm aware,
I treat everyone that way.

432
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:56,649
That's just how it looks to you.

433
00:29:56,650 --> 00:29:57,819
The way I see it,

434
00:29:57,820 --> 00:30:01,580
you're only awkward when it
comes to things dealing with yourself.

435
00:30:02,330 --> 00:30:06,040
You're much smoother when it comes
to others, which is why no one notices.

436
00:30:07,290 --> 00:30:10,079
So, have you finally remembered?

437
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:12,250
Do you know which
Heroic Spirit you are?

438
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,759
If you have some
connection to Saber,

439
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:17,590
you ought to be from an
era that's close to hers, right?

440
00:30:18,260 --> 00:30:20,930
No. Everything is still hazy.

441
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:25,430
But as you say, I do have
memories of this Saber.

442
00:30:25,930 --> 00:30:30,810
However, she does not seem to know
me, so we could not have been very close.

443
00:30:31,810 --> 00:30:32,810
Oh.

444
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:37,320
More to the point,
Rin, how is your guest?

445
00:30:38,860 --> 00:30:41,529
Luckily, he wasn't
hit anywhere vital.

446
00:30:41,530 --> 00:30:45,159
But his wounds aren't
healing at all this time.

447
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,659
Their pact has been broken,

448
00:30:46,660 --> 00:30:49,870
so he might have lost the healing
ability he'd been getting from Saber.

449
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:54,880
No, not him. I meant the other.

450
00:30:56,380 --> 00:30:58,510
Oh, Fujimura-sensei?

451
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:02,219
Caster seems to have put
her under a sleeping spell,

452
00:31:02,220 --> 00:31:05,059
but she's perfectly healthy.

453
00:31:05,060 --> 00:31:09,230
I've treated her, so she could
sleep a whole week with no problems.

454
00:31:10,850 --> 00:31:14,109
Knowing Fujimura-sensei, she
might jump out of bed any moment.

455
00:31:14,110 --> 00:31:18,819
Perhaps, but that woman's
enchantments are more curses than spells.

456
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:22,449
The simplest way to break
them is to kill the original caster.

457
00:31:22,450 --> 00:31:23,530
That's true.

458
00:31:33,420 --> 00:31:36,419
Defeating Caster
is our top priority.

459
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:37,839
I know.

460
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:41,760
If possible, I'd like to do so before
Saber falls completely under her control.

461
00:31:43,510 --> 00:31:44,760
Understood.

462
00:31:45,100 --> 00:31:49,099
So your pact with that
boy is also over, then.

463
00:31:49,100 --> 00:31:50,100
What?

464
00:31:50,230 --> 00:31:51,560
Don't "what" me.

465
00:31:52,310 --> 00:31:55,270
Emiya Shirou is no
longer a Master, correct?

466
00:31:55,650 --> 00:31:57,269
What's this?

467
00:31:57,270 --> 00:32:02,820
Surely you aren't going to say that you
mean to look after him as a fallen comrade.

468
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:08,029
Hardly. I'm not that soft.

469
00:32:08,030 --> 00:32:09,030
What, then?

470
00:32:09,290 --> 00:32:11,660
It isn't over yet.

471
00:32:12,620 --> 00:32:16,959
Our agreement will stand until he
himself says that he wants out of the war.

472
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,709
I can reject him all I want,

473
00:32:18,710 --> 00:32:22,970
but nothing is over
until he says it is.

474
00:32:25,470 --> 00:32:26,470
Rin...

475
00:32:27,140 --> 00:32:29,599
That's our course of action.

476
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:31,480
Do you object, Archer?

477
00:32:32,430 --> 00:32:34,309
Would it matter if I did?

478
00:32:34,310 --> 00:32:38,650
I know painfully well that you
won't stop until you have your way.

479
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:42,150
Let's go, Archer!

480
00:32:51,540 --> 00:32:52,540
Huh?

481
00:32:54,370 --> 00:32:55,830
Where am I?

482
00:33:06,720 --> 00:33:09,970
Nobody's... here?

483
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:20,110
Which means that she's
out there... by herself...

484
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:32,870
Sorry... I made a
mess... Tohsaka.

485
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:41,550
This...

486
00:33:42,130 --> 00:33:43,260
looks familiar...

487
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:47,680
Oh, right. It's the same
as the one from that night.

488
00:33:47,970 --> 00:33:50,099
Don't do this to me...

489
00:33:50,100 --> 00:33:51,969
Why did it have to be you?

490
00:33:51,970 --> 00:33:55,980
Why did you have to pick this
hour, on this day, to be here?

491
00:33:57,350 --> 00:33:59,560
No. There's still a way.

492
00:34:04,610 --> 00:34:07,610
Damn it... What the hell?

493
00:34:08,150 --> 00:34:11,320
She's always going on
about debts and favors,

494
00:34:12,870 --> 00:34:16,540
but this is one debt
I can never repay!

495
00:34:24,670 --> 00:34:25,840
Tohsaka...

496
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:41,020
Are you listening, Assassin?

497
00:34:41,770 --> 00:34:45,729
I believe I instructed you to
continue guarding the front gate.

498
00:34:45,730 --> 00:34:48,490
There was an intruder, you see.

499
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:51,570
I spotted an unusual
bird, so I struck it down.

500
00:34:51,990 --> 00:34:54,160
Is this something
used by your kind?

501
00:34:54,490 --> 00:34:57,500
Yes. It is a familiar
used for espionage.

502
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:02,669
That young lady
has terrible luck.

503
00:35:02,670 --> 00:35:07,380
If she were slightly less talented, I
would have taken her on as my pupil.

504
00:35:08,260 --> 00:35:11,179
I leave my Master's
defense to you, Assassin.

505
00:35:11,180 --> 00:35:13,389
Guard the gate
with your very life.

506
00:35:13,390 --> 00:35:20,230
Ever since I've been summoned,
I, Kojirou, have never truly felt alive.

507
00:35:20,940 --> 00:35:24,610
Ordering such a person to do
or die is meaningless, is it not?

508
00:35:25,110 --> 00:35:26,610
Don't quibble.

509
00:35:27,030 --> 00:35:30,069
You are a Servant
that I summoned.

510
00:35:30,070 --> 00:35:34,740
If you cannot pledge fealty to your lord,
I shall simply eliminate you right now.

511
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:37,620
I see. Goodness me.

512
00:35:38,620 --> 00:35:41,056
My life is as insubstantial
as a shimmering heat haze,

513
00:35:41,068 --> 00:35:43,380
but I would rather it not
be extinguished just yet.

514
00:35:44,420 --> 00:35:48,379
After all, I do have
a promise to keep.

515
00:35:48,380 --> 00:35:51,419
Then hold your tongue.

516
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:54,390
Your only concern
is guarding this place.

517
00:35:55,550 --> 00:35:57,929
Then guard it I shall.

518
00:35:57,930 --> 00:36:00,100
But is this wise, Caster?

519
00:36:00,430 --> 00:36:05,230
I am also disloyal to my lord, but you are
acting on your own authority far too often.

520
00:36:05,690 --> 00:36:09,360
Your errand tonight is also without
your Master's knowledge, I'd wager.

521
00:36:13,860 --> 00:36:19,620
Day by day, you overstep your
bounds ever further, Caster...

522
00:36:19,910 --> 00:36:23,829
Silence. The next time
you make me repeat myself,

523
00:36:23,830 --> 00:36:26,880
I'll eliminate you without
waiting out the next five days.

524
00:36:27,170 --> 00:36:32,009
Oh, dear. They say that women
and children are difficult to deal with.

525
00:36:32,010 --> 00:36:33,760
It would appear
that is indeed true.

526
00:36:37,430 --> 00:36:40,640
Worry not. I understand.

527
00:36:40,970 --> 00:36:44,979
This is all to be carried out without
your Master's knowledge, yes?

528
00:36:44,980 --> 00:36:47,269
Yours is a touching tale.

529
00:36:47,270 --> 00:36:52,649
I only hope that your love
for your lord should reach him.

530
00:36:52,650 --> 00:36:54,899
Assassin, mind your...

531
00:36:54,900 --> 00:36:56,819
I am a sore loser.

532
00:36:56,820 --> 00:36:59,160
Allow me these witless jests.

533
00:36:59,530 --> 00:37:00,910
On my blade,

534
00:37:01,330 --> 00:37:04,119
I swear I shall protect this gate
from all, no matter who they be.

535
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:06,920
But where might you be going?

536
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:09,750
Do you not trust my protection?

537
00:37:10,090 --> 00:37:14,089
Of course not. You are
merely my insurance.

538
00:37:14,090 --> 00:37:15,929
But I no longer
require that, either.

539
00:37:15,930 --> 00:37:21,260
With Saber now mine, I no longer need
to make this rustic place my sanctuary.

540
00:37:21,890 --> 00:37:23,769
A change of location?

541
00:37:23,770 --> 00:37:27,310
Meaning that you have
no further use for me.

542
00:37:28,020 --> 00:37:30,519
There is a sacred spot
superior to this mountain?

543
00:37:30,520 --> 00:37:34,570
Yes. A place which
suits me perfectly.

544
00:37:35,950 --> 00:37:39,409
I will be leaving to claim
my prize ahead of schedule.

545
00:37:39,410 --> 00:37:41,620
I now have a new
fortification, the Grail,

546
00:37:42,160 --> 00:37:45,249
and even a new pawn
in the form of Saber.

547
00:37:45,250 --> 00:37:48,039
With all these, even my
reticent Master will be unable

548
00:37:48,051 --> 00:37:50,540
to offer up any objections
to my plan of action.

549
00:37:51,090 --> 00:37:55,169
Once I have the Grail, I
will have nothing to fear.

550
00:37:55,170 --> 00:38:00,550
Yes, for then none will be able to stand
against me, no matter who they may be!

551
00:38:18,700 --> 00:38:19,989
Caster.

552
00:38:19,990 --> 00:38:25,329
Have we met before, my
good overseer of this mad ritual?

553
00:38:25,330 --> 00:38:27,499
What do you want, Caster?

554
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:30,419
This place is inviolable
neutral territory.

555
00:38:30,420 --> 00:38:35,419
No Servant may enter this place, regardless
of which Heroic Spirit they may be.

556
00:38:35,420 --> 00:38:37,720
The rules have changed.

557
00:38:41,010 --> 00:38:42,470
Command Spells?

558
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:50,900
Saber...

559
00:38:51,150 --> 00:38:54,569
Saber is now my puppet.

560
00:38:54,570 --> 00:38:56,860
You understand what
that means, I take it?

561
00:38:57,150 --> 00:38:59,989
The outcome of this war
is as good as decided.

562
00:38:59,990 --> 00:39:04,120
Is there something wrong with
coming to claim my prize early?

563
00:39:04,450 --> 00:39:05,579
Indeed there is.

564
00:39:05,580 --> 00:39:09,959
The Grail will not appear
until but one Servant remains.

565
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:14,919
As a Servant, surely you were made aware
of this at the time of your summoning.

566
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:17,919
Yes, the Grail did say that.

567
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:20,166
It ordered me to go
forth and slay the other

568
00:39:20,178 --> 00:39:22,179
Heroic Spirits in
order to activate it.

569
00:39:22,180 --> 00:39:23,180
However,

570
00:39:23,390 --> 00:39:25,890
that refers to the
Greater Grail, does it not?

571
00:39:27,310 --> 00:39:30,599
Tell me, where is
the Lesser Grail?

572
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:34,440
You priests are in charge of
the Grail's key, are you not?

573
00:39:36,610 --> 00:39:38,989
There is no Holy Grail here.

574
00:39:38,990 --> 00:39:41,280
Do you wish to die?

575
00:39:42,740 --> 00:39:44,160
Don't make idle threats.

576
00:39:44,870 --> 00:39:47,830
You betray yourself,
Princess of Colchis.

577
00:39:48,160 --> 00:39:52,040
You still have no stomach
for brutality, do you?

578
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:57,360
You just want me to
stand by and watch, right?

579
00:40:57,770 --> 00:40:59,520
No one's going to interfere.

580
00:41:04,570 --> 00:41:08,370
This era has fine
warriors too, I see.

581
00:41:10,700 --> 00:41:14,710
But how long will his
fighting spirit last, I wonder?

582
00:41:38,770 --> 00:41:41,820
Tohsaka... Where are you?

583
00:42:04,300 --> 00:42:06,670
Why are you here?

584
00:42:10,220 --> 00:42:11,600
Go home.

585
00:42:12,010 --> 00:42:15,929
I don't know what you're trying to
prove, but you're being a nuisance.

586
00:42:15,930 --> 00:42:17,599
I'm not going anywhere.

587
00:42:17,600 --> 00:42:20,400
I promised that I'd fight
alongside you, remember?

588
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:23,320
Forget about that
stupid promise.

589
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:27,400
I mean, what can you
possibly do as you are now?

590
00:42:27,780 --> 00:42:30,159
You've lost Saber.

591
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,280
I...

592
00:42:32,030 --> 00:42:35,870
Besides, there's no
need for you to fight now.

593
00:42:36,660 --> 00:42:38,749
You're not a Master anymore.

594
00:42:38,750 --> 00:42:40,629
Take shelter in the
church, and you'll be safe.

595
00:42:40,630 --> 00:42:45,459
Don't be stupid! I can't
leave Saber like that!

596
00:42:45,460 --> 00:42:49,220
So no matter what, I'm
gonna fight to the bitter en...

597
00:42:51,140 --> 00:42:52,889
Look at yourself.

598
00:42:52,890 --> 00:42:57,310
You've had Saber to help you until
now, but you're a wreck without her.

599
00:43:01,150 --> 00:43:04,359
Besides, for all your
talk about Saber,

600
00:43:04,360 --> 00:43:07,110
what happens to her is
no longer your concern.

601
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:10,659
You're wrong. I may
not be a Master anymore,

602
00:43:10,660 --> 00:43:13,570
but I could tell
she was in anguish.

603
00:43:13,950 --> 00:43:17,909
I won't leave her
in Caster's grasp!

604
00:43:17,910 --> 00:43:18,960
I see.

605
00:43:19,580 --> 00:43:21,870
The problem is,
you're powerless.

606
00:43:22,670 --> 00:43:28,920
If you refuse to admit
it, I'll tell you straight:

607
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:33,930
there's nothing you can do
to help Saber as you are now.

608
00:43:37,770 --> 00:43:39,729
That's all there is to say.

609
00:43:39,730 --> 00:43:43,190
You've lost Saber, and
you're no longer a Master.

610
00:43:43,810 --> 00:43:48,439
There's no longer any reason for you
to remain involved in the Holy Grail War,

611
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:50,030
so bow out here.

612
00:43:50,530 --> 00:43:52,280
Hold up, Tohsaka!

613
00:43:52,570 --> 00:43:53,820
That may be true, but...

614
00:43:57,310 --> 00:43:59,530
- Your dream for the
future - yume ni miteita

615
00:43:57,830 --> 00:43:59,540
What are you
thinking, you idiot?

616
00:44:00,300 --> 00:44:01,385
Seems unattainable

617
00:44:01,386 --> 00:44:02,470
ano hi no kage ni

618
00:44:03,850 --> 00:44:06,225
even through all your toil

619
00:44:06,226 --> 00:44:08,600
todokanai sakebi

620
00:44:09,270 --> 00:44:10,760
No matter what you do,

621
00:44:10,761 --> 00:44:12,249
asu no jibun wa

622
00:44:12,250 --> 00:44:13,615
you cannot give up

623
00:44:13,616 --> 00:44:14,980
nante egaite mo

624
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:18,570
on hoping for brighter days

625
00:44:18,571 --> 00:44:21,380
kienai negai ni nureru

626
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:27,555
In your hand you hold

627
00:44:27,556 --> 00:44:30,270
koboreochiru kakera wo

628
00:44:30,780 --> 00:44:33,155
the fragments of our lives

629
00:44:33,156 --> 00:44:35,530
tsukamu sono te de

630
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:39,420
Stay your heart of doubt

631
00:44:39,421 --> 00:44:42,040
yureru kokoro kakaete

632
00:44:42,790 --> 00:44:46,415
and soar through the night

633
00:44:46,416 --> 00:44:50,040
tobikonda ike yoru he

634
00:44:51,420 --> 00:44:54,440
Relying on others

635
00:44:54,441 --> 00:44:57,459
dareka wo ate ni shitemo

636
00:44:57,460 --> 00:45:00,455
will not help you
find your true self

637
00:45:00,456 --> 00:45:03,449
motomeru mono ja nai no dakara

638
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:06,375
Dispel this illusion

639
00:45:06,376 --> 00:45:09,299
hontou no jibun
wa koko ni iru tte

640
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:13,685
and open your eyes

641
00:45:13,686 --> 00:45:18,070
me wo tojite inaide

642
00:45:14,360 --> 00:45:16,070
Stay out of this from here on,

643
00:45:16,820 --> 00:45:18,070
or you're dead.

644
00:45:39,190 --> 00:45:41,300
The wind spreads

645
00:45:42,230 --> 00:45:44,040
long-forgotten smiles

646
00:45:45,790 --> 00:45:50,300
like dusty old paper

647
00:45:51,080 --> 00:45:53,890
Praying for the power

648
00:45:54,270 --> 00:45:56,430
to accomplish more tomorrow

649
00:45:57,750 --> 00:46:03,360
is only making it harder for you

650
00:46:06,790 --> 00:46:12,340
Your body has grown hard as ice

651
00:46:12,680 --> 00:46:16,850
even as your dream is budding

652
00:46:18,780 --> 00:46:24,150
Fly towards the dawn

653
00:46:24,790 --> 00:46:32,390
before you turn to ash

654
00:46:33,470 --> 00:46:38,760
Relying on others

655
00:46:39,450 --> 00:46:45,330
will not help you
find your true self

656
00:46:45,430 --> 00:46:51,250
Dispel this illusion

657
00:46:51,510 --> 00:46:56,540
and open your eyes

658
00:46:57,390 --> 00:47:02,790
Isn't it enough to
live for the moment

659
00:47:03,420 --> 00:47:09,360
and dedicate it to others

660
00:47:09,500 --> 00:47:15,280
Abandon your pretense

661
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:23,480
and be yourself

662
00:47:35,420 --> 00:47:38,169
Will you be able to believe you made
the right choices until the very end?

663
00:47:38,170 --> 00:47:40,009
No, I comprehend the situation.

664
00:47:40,010 --> 00:47:42,259
Has the matter
outside been resolved?

665
00:47:42,260 --> 00:47:43,260
Shirou, get back!

666
